  - CHANGELOG.md
learnings:
  - 'A ''param accepted but ignored by the reader'' bug recurs in this codebase: the writer computes the right value (resolveActivePack → packRoot) and the reader silently uses a different default (ctx.rootDir → project index). Same shape as the v6.6.2 pm_postflight and v6.6.3 flow_check bugs. When a selector/param exists, grep that the READER actually consumes it.'
  - 'University packs ship content under TWO layouts: project/discipline packs use content/, the first-party pack uses src/content/. Any pack-content code must probe both — and the probe logic is itself duplicated (countPackEntries vs the new resolveContentBase), a latent drift filed as T-2026-05-31-001.'
  - Non-project University packs have no index.yaml, so pack-aware reads must scan content in-memory, not assume a prebuilt index.
  - Authoring a real artifact (the ai-literacy pack) surfaced a framework bug that internal testing missed — dog-fooding the multi-tenant pack feature is what exposed the selector gap.
